message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Hardware Friction Scorecard Dataset: Quantitative Analysis of Neural Architecture Adoption (2017-2025)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025-12-10
authors:
  - family-names: Lambropoulos
    given-names: Petros
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/petroslamb/hardware-friction-scorecard-dataset"
url: "https://github.com/petroslamb/hardware-friction-scorecard-dataset"
abstract: >
  A quantitative dataset scoring 119+ neural network architectures (2017-2025)
  against the Hardware Friction Scorecard rubric. Each architecture is evaluated
  on five axes: Global Access (GA), Memory Access Locality (MAL), Parallelism (PAR),
  Specialized Tooling Investment (STI), and Infrastructure Maturity (IM). These
  scores predict production adoption by measuring hardware compatibility and
  ecosystem friction. The dataset includes Transformers, State-Space Models, MoE,
  Multimodal architectures (image/video/audio), and historical baselines.
keywords:
  - neural architecture
  - hardware compatibility
  - transformer
  - adoption prediction
  - GPU optimization
  - machine learning infrastructure
  - production ML
